135:### `web_fetch`
136-
137:`web_fetch` fetches URLs from the app runtime. It follows up to ten redirects and checks every destination for SSRF safety. Non-success responses return plain text with the response body when available.
138-
139-```sh
140:eve add tool/web_fetch
141-```
142-
143:```ts title="agent/tools/web_fetch.ts"
144:export { default } from "eve/tools/web_fetch";
145-```
146-
147-Override it:
148-
149:```ts title="agent/tools/web_fetch.ts"
150-import { defineTool } from "eve/tools";
151:import { webFetch } from "eve/tools/web_fetch";
152-
153-export default defineTool({
154-  ...webFetch,
155-  description: "Fetch approved public documentation URLs.",
156-  async execute(input, ctx) {
157-    const hostname = new URL(input.url).hostname;
158-    if (hostname !== "docs.example.com") {
159:      throw new Error("web_fetch is limited to docs.example.com");
160-    }
161-    return webFetch.execute(input, ctx);
162-  },
163-});
164-```
165-
166-Disable it:
167-
168:```ts title="agent/tools/web_fetch.ts"
169-import { disableTool } from "eve/tools";
170-
171-export default disableTool();
172-```
173-
174-### `web_search`
175-
176-`web_search` uses provider-managed web search and appears only for supported model providers. AI Gateway models use Exa by default; direct provider models use their native search implementation.
177-
178-```sh
179-eve add tool/web_search
180-```
